{"type":"text","timestamp":1794255820015,"sessionID":"ses_e3e0f3005ffelmLWIfqr9T6x4h","part":{"id":"prt_1c1fb14da0018ToMmPuPFoIiWj","messageID":"msg_1c1fae725001mFUa9l29Rgdd9w","sessionID":"ses_e3e0f3005ffelmLWIfqr9T6x4h","type":"text","text":"I built the recipe book on top of the starter project. I tested the API with curl against gunicorn and checked that the frontend builds (`npm run build`, including the TypeScript check). I couldn't build or run the Docker image because Docker isn't installed here. I also didn't try the web pages in a browser, since no headless browser was available.\n\n**What I checked with curl:**\n- The four sample recipes appear on first start and are still there after a restart.\n- Register, login and the 401 without a valid token.\n- Validation errors are returned field by field.\n- A non-author gets 403 when editing or deleting.\n- Filtering by category and searching titles works, and paging is newest first.\n- Ingredients come back in the order given.\n- The server also serves the built frontend, including direct links to recipe pages.\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`):\n- Data is stored in SQLite at `./data/app.db`.\n- Login tokens are random strings saved in the database, so a signed-in user stays signed in after a restart. Passwords are stored hashed.\n- The four sample recipes are in three categories (Breakfast, Main, Dessert). They belong to a built-in user `chef` with a random password, so nobody can sign in as it to edit or delete them.\n\n**Rules I chose where the spec was silent:**\n- Usernames are 3–32 letters, digits, `.`, `_` or `-`, and are not case-sensitive. Passwords are 6–128 characters.\n- A username that's already taken gets 409.\n- Validation errors come back as 400 with an overall message and a message per field, which the forms show next to each field.\n- A missing recipe gets 404. An invalid `page` gets 400. `page_size` defaults to 12 and is capped at 100.\n- The category and title filters ignore case.\n\n**Endpoints I added beyond the spec:** `POST /api/auth/logout`, `GET /api/auth/me` and `GET /api/categories` (which fills the category dropdown).\n\n**Frontend** (React, TypeScript and Tailwind 4; the only CSS file is Tailwind's entry file `src/index.css`):\n- **Sign-in:** registration and sign-in forms, plus the username and a sign-out button in the header.\n- **Recipe list:** cards with a category dropdown, a title search and Previous/Next paging. Filters and page are kept in the URL.\n- **Recipe page:** ingredients as a list and instructions with line breaks kept. Edit and Delete appear only for the author, and Delete asks for confirmation.\n- **Add/edit forms:** ingredient rows can be added, removed and moved up or down.\n\n**Dependency changes:** I added `tailwindcss`, `@tailwindcss/vite`, `typescript` and the React type packages, and updated the lock file. `npm run build` now runs the TypeScript check before building, and `npm run typecheck` runs it alone. I also added a `.gitignore`. The Dockerfile is unchanged.","time":{"start":1794255819994,"end":1794255819997}}}
